According to Microsoft's official documentation, WinAppDriver is no longer under active development, and Microsoft recommends moving to Appium with the Windows Application Driver plugin.

However, the original Appium Windows Driver has also been deprecated. The Appium project now identifies Appium WinCore Driver as its official replacement.

For new Windows 11 desktop automation projects, we should evaluate WinCore Driver rather than adopt the legacy WinAppDriver stack.

References:

- Microsoft: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/apps/develop/testing/#ui-test-automation
- Appium deprecation notice: https://github.com/appium/appium-windows-driver
- WinCore Driver: https://github.com/appium/appium-wincore-driver
